# red-team, S4 Stage-3 review, Finding 6 (Issue #75) / architecture-reviewer Finding 5 (Issue #78):
# this repo had no line-ending policy at all — on a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true), git
# converts previously-tracked files to CRLF on ordinary operations (checkout/stash/pull/merge)
# while brand-new untracked files stay LF, producing a silent split that broke
# src/qa/shell-detector-mutants.ts's byte-literal multi-line anchor matching. Force LF for the
# source/text files this project's own tooling reads byte-for-byte, so that class of drift cannot
# recur regardless of a contributor's local git config. (shell-detector-mutants.ts's own
# `normalizeLineEndings` closes the same gap independently at the matching layer — both are kept,
# per both review reports' "either is sufficient alone" recommendation.)
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
